  "policy": "verbatim copies (one listed edit, see files[thick/common/nets.py].edits) of the import closure of the official THICK world model (ContextRSSM / GateL0RD, THICKNet, losses, optimizer), the THICK Dreamer agent and the VisualPinPad training entry points (train.py, train_from_replay.py, train_only_on_replay.py). Upstream layout kept (thick/...); upstream uses top-level imports (import common), so callers put vendor/thick on sys.path, as upstream does. Run only in env b127-thick-tf (TF 2.4.2); never imported by the PyTorch port.",
  "runtime_notes": [
    "Not vendored: thick/multiworld/ (MuJoCo Sawyer suite + assets), common/{minihack_utils,multiworld_utils,minigrid_utils,plot}.py, des_envs/, media/ (imported upstream only inside the MiniHack / MiniGrid / Multiworld branches of env_register).",
    "Upstream defect, not edited: common/dists.py OneHotDist._pad ignores its tensor argument and returns probs, so get_logits() returns probabilities; the CCEL_logits action loss (VisualPinPad / MiniHack discrete actions) is therefore a softmax cross-entropy on probabilities. The PyTorch port reproduces this behaviour.",
    "train.py / train_from_replay.py assert a visible GPU; the CPU smoke (scripts/b127_thick_port_reference.py --official-smoke) stubs that query at run time without editing the file."
  ],
